## Changing queries

Data access is generated by [sqlc](https://docs.sqlc.dev/) from
`{{.Slots.store.Dir}}/queries.sql` and the schema in
`{{.Slots.database.Dir}}/{{index .Traits "sql-schema"}}`, with sqlc's
`{{index .Traits "sql-dialect"}}` engine, so write queries in that SQL dialect;
`sqlc.arg(name)` declares a parameter in any dialect. The generated code in
`{{.Slots.store.Dir}}/sqlcgen` is committed; do not edit it by hand. After
changing the schema or the queries, regenerate it with `make generate`, or
without make:

```sh
go run github.com/sqlc-dev/sqlc/cmd/sqlc@{{index .Versions "github.com/sqlc-dev/sqlc"}} generate
```

The CI workflow runs `sqlc diff` and fails when the committed code is not
what sqlc generates from the queries and the schema.
